SUMMARY:Jewish without Apology: A Conversation with Sarah Hurwitz
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260426T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260426T170000
DTSTAMP:20260422T210317Z
UID:TU2025222010
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260426T150000
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260115T234631Z
DESCRIPTION:**Seth Goodchild Memorial Lecture**  \nReception immediately f
 ollowing  \n  \nEvent is at capacity. To be added to the waiting list\, co
 ntact: Email Aviva Arad\, aarad@shomrei.org  \n  \n**LIVESTREAM  \nThis ev
 ent will be livestreamed but NOT recorded. To watch remotely\, you must tu
 ne in at the time of the event:  http://shomrei.org/live: https://shomrei.
 org/live**  \n  \n**About the Program**  \nAward-winning author Sarah Hurw
 itz joins Rabbi Julie Roth for a candid conversation about rediscovering J
 udaism as an adult and why its intellectual depth and moral clarity feel s
 trikingly relevant to modern life. From finding meaning in a chaotic world
  to standing tall against rising antisemitism\, Sarah explores why embraci
 ng Jewish wisdom isn’t just about honoring the past -- it’s about sanc
 tifying the present and elevating our shared humanity.   \n  \n**Free Baby
 sitting Available**  \nEmail Aviva Arad\, aarad@shomrei.org  \n  \n**\\*Ad
 ditional parking is available next door at 73 &amp\; 77 Park Street.**  \n
   \n**In Loving Memory of Seth Goodchild**   \nSeth Goodchild was inspired
  by his family to convert to Judaism at the end of his life. To honor his 
 legacy and share his love of Judaism\, his friends and family sponsored th
 is lecture and a class on exploring Judaism.\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260421T131353Z
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL;VALUE=URI:https://teamup.com/kstx8swyw669kakgqa/events/2025222010
X-SOURCE:Congregation Shomrei Emunah
END:VEVENT
